WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:06.050
The Game of Thrones Season 7 finale begins
with Daenerys’ army arriving at King’s

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.050
Landing.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.099
This is as close as Dany has ever come to
her goal of the Iron Throne.

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:15.500
She could probably swoop in and take it now,
but she’s holding off in the hopes of a

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.500
truce.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.350
In her vision in Season 2, Dany approaches
the Throne, and reaches for it, but doesn’t

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:22.400
take it.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.289
Maybe this suggests that Dany will never win
the Throne.

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:30.160
Jaime and Bronn watch from above and talk
about the meaning of life.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.530
Is it gold?

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.530
Family?

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.530
Cocks?

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:37.470
Bronn is one of the few characters in Thrones
who’s actually better off now than he was

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.730
in Season 1.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.410
He’s made money, been knighted, got people
calling him “my lord”.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:48.640
While so many others have lost loved ones,
or lost their heads, or their hands, or their

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:49.640
cocks.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.250
Jon Snow also arrives at King’s Landing.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.260
When his uncle Ned came to this city, he died.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:59.030
When Ned’s father and brother came to this
city, they died too.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:04.170
The Starks are never comfortable in the crowded
capital – Jaime once said Starks are made

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:10.360
of ice, and when they come south, they melt
. But, as we soon learn, Jon is more than

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.090
just a Stark.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.750
The groups meet in the ruins of the Dragonpit.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:19.060
The Dragonpit was built a few hundred years
ago as a sort of a stable for the Targaryen

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:24.920
dragons . But as Daenerys learned in Meereen,
dragons don’t like captivity . Over the

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:30.720
years, the pit dragons grew smaller and stunted
, which reflects the slow decline of the Targaryen

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.810
dynasty.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.760
It also reflects the nature of magic in Game
of Thrones.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:41.780
Magic is wild and uncontrollable, a sword
with no hilt . If you lock a dragon in a box,

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:42.780
it’ll waste away.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:47.880
But if you let it loose, it’ll eat people
. So there’s no safe way to use it.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.810
Which is why some people think that the maesters
of the Citadel may have deliberately killed

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:57.470
off the dragons as part of a conspiracy against
magic – go watch that video.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:01.350
But everyone comes together in the biggest
meeting of characters ever.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:06.469
Tyrion reunites with Bronn and Pod – who
have both saved his life in the past.

00:02:06.469 --> 00:02:11.190
Brienne and the Hound talk about Arya like
proud soccer moms, even though Brienne almost

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.190
killed Sandor once.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.550
Other reunions aren’t so happy.

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:19.590
Tyrion sees his sister Cersei – after he
killed their father Tywin.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:23.000
Daenerys meets Jaime, who killed her father
Aerys.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.510
Theon sees Euron, who captured his sister
Yara.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:29.660
And Jon meets Cersei who helped kill his uncle
Ned.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:35.370
There’s also this awkward love… square
between Brienne Jaime Cersei and Euron.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:39.550
So all of this history makes for a very tense
scene.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.280
Bronn leaves early, with Pod.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.270
Tyrion had just offered Bronn gold if he changes
sides , and Bronn always said he looks after

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.680
himself and doesn’t wanna risk his life
fighting dragons.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.680
So it looks likely that Bronn will leave Cersei
and maybe join Daenerys.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.440
But another possible reason why Bronn leaves
is that there’s apparently drama between

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.069
Bronn’s actor and Cersei’s actress, they
don’t wanna be in the same scenes .

00:03:02.069 --> 00:03:06.280
The Hound threatens the Mountain, which all
but confirms Cleganebowl – the idea that

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.870
these brothers will fight to the death in
the greatest grudge match in Westeros.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:15.850
Sandor has always wanted to kill his brother
. They fought once in Season 1, and it looks

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:18.890
like they’ll fight a final time in Season
8.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:23.540
Since Gregor is now some kinda zombie, the
Hound might need to use fire to kill him.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.930
Which might allow Sandor to get over his fear
of fire, which he got from Gregor burning

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.160
his face in the first place.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:35.709
So Cleganebowl is kinda silly, but it could
give a neat sense of closure to Sandor’s

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:36.709
story.

00:03:36.709 --> 00:03:41.060
Daenerys arrives on her dragon – you can
tell she’s been practicing her impressive

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:45.510
entrances – and Euron gets a hungry look
seeing the dragon.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:49.650
There’s a whole plot in the books about
Euron trying to use a magic horn to steal

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:54.379
one of Dany’s dragons . Maybe he’ll try
something similar in the show.

00:03:54.379 --> 00:03:59.260
Dany apologises for arriving late, and making
everyone wait , which is bit of a meta joke

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:04.239
about the fact it’s taken Dany seven seasons
to join the main plot in Westeros.

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:08.970
Tyrion starts a speech, but Euron interrupts
and gets all aggressive, and threatens to

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.519
kill Yara, but Cersei shushes him.

00:04:11.519 --> 00:04:16.140
Cersei might actually have told Euron to this,
because it’s useful to remind Dany’s side

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:21.100
that Cersei has a hostage, but shushing Euron’s
threat also makes Cersei look cooperative.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:26.110
It’s kinda the opposite of how Littlefinger
uses Lyn Corbray in Book 4 – for those who

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.850
are keeping score.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:31.530
Jon shows everyone the zombie, which is the
first time most of these people have seen

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:32.530
a wight.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:36.970
Tyrion, Varys, Missandei, Theon, Brienne,
Jaime, Cersei – they’ve all been mostly

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:39.930
separate from the supernatural in this story.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:44.030
But now magic and politics come crashing together.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:47.490
Jon explains the threat of the army of the
dead.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.720
With Qyburn it’s love at first sight.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.590
But everyone else is suitably spooked.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:57.160
Euron says he’ll retreat to the Iron Islands
– which is a lie designed by Cersei to make

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:01.680
Dany think Euron’s out of the picture, when
he’s actually getting more soldiers for

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:02.680
Cersei.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:07.190
Cersei says she’s convinced, and agrees
to a peace on one condition – Jon has to

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:10.810
swear to stay out of the war between Cersei
and Dany.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:15.160
So this is a good strategy from Cersei – she’s
hoping to take away Dany’s greatest ally,

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:20.030
and let Dany fight the dead, while Cersei
gathers her strength to later fight a weakened

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.030
Dany.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.650
But Jon refuses Cersei’s deal, and Cersei
stomps out.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:28.911
Brienne tries to get Jaime to change Cersei’s
mind, telling him “Fuck loyalty”, which

00:05:28.911 --> 00:05:34.350
is a neat reversal of their usual dynamic,
with oathkeeping Brienne trying to teach honour

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.800
to Jaime the Kingslayer.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:41.289
But the job of convincing Cersei falls to
the man who Cersei hates most – her brother

00:05:41.289 --> 00:05:42.330
Tyrion.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:47.110
Cersei starts out hating Tyrion for a lot
of the same reasons their father Tywin hated

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:51.920
Tyrion – for the death of Tyrion’s mother
in childbirth, and for Tyrion’s mockery

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.220
of their family pride.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:58.310
But Cersei’s hatred of Tyrion grows through
the series as he undermines her power, threatens

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:01.919
her and her children, and sends Myrcella to
Dorne.

00:06:01.919 --> 00:06:06.750
In Season 4 Cersei accuses him of killing
Joffrey, which he didn’t, but then he kills

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.880
Tywin – and ever since, Cersei’s tried
to have Tyrion killed.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:15.520
Cersei accuses him of wanting to destroy their
family – even though Cersei has killed more

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:20.110
Lannisters than Tyrion has – she blew up
uncle Kevan and cousin Lancel.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:24.760
It’s true that the murder of Tywin was a
huge blow to House Lannister.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:29.060
But at least in the beginning, it wasn’t
Tyrion’s goal to destroy his family.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:32.330
He loved Jaime, and he loved Myrcella and
Tommen.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.840
And deep down, Cersei must know this.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.920
Cause when Tyrion tells her to kill him, she
doesn’t.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.880
Or maybe she only wants him alive to make
this peace deal.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.860
Cersei says she doesn’t care about the world,
doesn’t care about anyone but herself and

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.319
the people she loves.

00:06:48.319 --> 00:06:53.420
Tyrion works out she’s pregnant, the scene
ends, and they make the peace deal.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:57.729
So we don’t know exactly what happens here,
but it seems Cersei uses her pregnancy to

00:06:57.729 --> 00:07:01.970
show that she’s got something to lose, to
make Cersei more believable when she says

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:02.980
that she’ll make peace.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:08.069
It’s similar to when Cersei used her pregnancy
to assure Jaime’s loyalty – she’s using

00:07:08.069 --> 00:07:10.280
her body as a strategic tool.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:16.250
As Cersei once said, a woman’s weapon is
between her legs . As always, Cersei uses

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:20.120
her weapon to protect her power and pride.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:24.270
Some people think that Tyrion might have offered
Cersei something to convince her to make peace

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:28.340
– like maybe that her child could be the
heir to the Throne or something.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:31.680
But does Cersei have much leverage in this
situation anyway?

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:36.650
It’s in her interests to make peace even
if she gets nothing in return – so there

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:40.280
may not have been a secret deal here between
Cersei and Tyrion.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:45.849
At the Dragonpit, Dany tells Jon that Mirri
Maz Duur said that Dany can’t have children,

00:07:45.849 --> 00:07:48.800
and Jon suggests that Mirri might have been
wrong.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:53.349
They keep on bringing up Dany’s fertility
– maybe she can have kids now.

00:07:53.349 --> 00:07:56.780
Maybe she always could, and Daario was just
shooting blanks.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:00.849
It could solve this whole succession problem
if Dany has a kid with Jon.

00:08:00.849 --> 00:08:05.130
And a pregnancy could also suggest that Dany
might actually survive this series – at

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.419
least, for another nine months.

00:08:07.419 --> 00:08:11.979
Cersei declares that she’ll make peace with
Dany and fight with her against the dead.

00:08:11.979 --> 00:08:17.710
But later we learn it was all a lie, and Cersei
will let Dany go north while she stays south

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:19.660
and gathers her strength.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:23.890
Jaime argues that they need to go help defeat
the dead, and that they won’t defeat Dany

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.490
in the long run anyway.

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:30.580
Cersei points out that Dany has lost a dragon,
which means she can be beat, and she reveals

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:35.610
that she sent Euron to Essos to hire a mercenary
group called the Golden Company using the

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.479
gold from Highgarden.

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:42.050
In the books, the Golden Company has a long
history , and they’re involved in Varys’

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:45.040
complex conspiracy – go watch that video.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:49.430
That sorta stuff won’t be in the show, but
they do have oliphants, so that’ll be dope.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:53.640
Point is, with the help of the Golden Company,
Cersei hopes to defeat Dany when she returns

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.089
from fighting the dead.

00:08:55.089 --> 00:08:56.519
But Jaime’s mad.

00:08:56.519 --> 00:08:59.210
He’s mad that Cersei didn’t tell him her
plan.

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:01.839
He’s mad that she’s talking about marrying
Euron.

00:09:01.839 --> 00:09:06.170
And most of all he’s mad about being forced
to break his word to help Dany – cause all

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:11.700
his life Jaime’s been hated for breaking
his Kingsguard oaths and killing King Aerys.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:16.780
Now, Jaime wants to ride with Aerys’ daughter,
and restore his honour – do something selfless

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:17.860
for once.

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:21.250
Jaime stood by Cersei when she tried to kill
his brother Tyrion.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:26.080
He stood by her when she killed Jaime’s
uncle and cousin and hundreds of innocents.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:31.209
But now Jaime realises that he can’t be
with Cersei and become the person he wants

00:09:31.209 --> 00:09:32.459
to be.

00:09:32.459 --> 00:09:34.459
And so he leaves.

00:09:34.459 --> 00:09:36.550
Jaime rides north.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:41.080
Instead of rich gold Lannister armour he wears
black and rides a black horse, maybe hinting

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.060
he could join the Night’s Watch someday.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.459
But Jaime’s final fate may be back at the
capital.

00:09:46.459 --> 00:09:51.089
He and Cersei often say that they’ll die
together – watch the Cersei video to see

00:09:51.089 --> 00:09:52.950
how that might end.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:56.460
As Jaime rides, snow falls on King’s Landing.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.570
Winter is here.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:03.200
Up at Winterfell, Littlefinger leads Sansa
to believe that Arya wants to kill Sansa and

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:08.170
become Lady of Winterfell – which Arya herself
kinda hinted last episode.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.829
And Sansa seems to believe Petyr.

00:10:09.829 --> 00:10:13.230
But later, she teams up with Arya and turns
against him.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:15.170
So… what changed?

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:19.330
Some people think that Sansa and Arya had
been secretly working together all along.

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:23.910
That these arguments they had last episode
were staged under the assumption that Littlefinger

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:28.279
would spy on them, so he would think his plan
to divide the sisters was working, while they

00:10:28.279 --> 00:10:30.610
actually plotted against him.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.210
But this idea isn’t really supported by
the show.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:36.790
It’s not clear what Sansa would gain by
leading Petyr along.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:41.350
There’s no evidence that Petyr would have
heard these multiple private conversations.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:45.040
And if Petyr was a good enough spy to see
these, wouldn’t he also have heard their

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.500
real plans?

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:50.491
An interview with Bran’s actor suggests
that these Sansa Arya scenes were real, but

00:10:50.491 --> 00:10:55.450
at some later point Sansa asked Bran for help
and he told her that Littlefinger misled them,

00:10:55.450 --> 00:11:01.680
and only then did Sansa team up with Arya
against Petyr . So there was no complex hidden

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:06.890
plot, the Starks were just really slow to
work out that Littlefinger was playing them.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:10.270
Even though Sansa already knew Littlefinger’s
been playing her.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:14.140
And even though Arya is a highly trained spy
and lie-detector.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:16.209
And even though Bran knows everything.

00:11:16.209 --> 00:11:20.339
So this whole plot was a pretty huge fail
from the Stark siblings.

00:11:20.339 --> 00:11:26.260
But they now realise that Petyr’s their
enemy, and accuse him his crimes – killing

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:31.709
Lysa, conspiring to kill Jon Arryn, lying
bout this dagger to cause war, betraying Ned,

00:11:31.709 --> 00:11:33.980
and giving Sansa to the Boltons.

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:38.780
Littlefinger falls to pieces, and totally
fails to defend himself, even though he probably

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:39.780
could.

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:44.180
The Starks have no hard evidence of Petyr’s
crimes, apart from the word of a crippled

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.720
boy who claims to be psychic.

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:50.620
Surely the master schemer Petyr could talk
his way out of this, just like how he talked

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:53.730
his way out of Lysa’s murder in the first
place.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:57.480
But he breaks down when he sees Sansa set
against him.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:02.360
He loves her so much – in his own creepy
way – that he just cannot deal with her

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:07.790
against him, and so he’s killed by Arya
– with the same blade Petyr used to start

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:10.160
this whole war in Season 1.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:15.950
Catelyn once said that Petyr is clever, but
not wise . He was clever enough to trick Sansa

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:21.360
and Arya, clever enough to cause a whole war,
but not wise enough to see his obsession with

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:25.070
Sansa was his blind spot and his downfall.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:29.550
And now Sansa has finally freed herself of
his control.

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:34.260
All series, she’s been a pawn of Cersei,
the Tyrells, Petyr, Ramsay.

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:39.200
But as Petyr says, “even the humblest pieces
can have wills of their own” . Sansa has

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:43.140
learned from the people who controlled her,
and freed herself at last.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:46.000
She’s her own person now, with her own power.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.700
We’ll see next season how she chooses to
use it.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:53.030
We also get a scene of Arya and Sansa being
friends again.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:57.160
Sansa quotes Ned saying “When the snows
fall and the white winds blow, the lone wolf

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:01.320
dies, but the pack survives” – Starks
gotta stick together.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:04.800
Might have been better advice if Ned said
“Hey if you’re thinking of murdering your

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:08.740
sister, ask your psychic brother first to
check if you’re being Littlefingered”

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:12.889
but it did work out in the end – the Starks
are united.

00:13:12.889 --> 00:13:17.840
At Dragonstone, Theon tells Jon about how
he felt growing up at Winterfell.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:23.040
He felt torn between his Greyjoy identity
and wanting to be part of the Stark family.

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:27.860
And that conflict led Theon to commit his
crimes – betraying the Starks, capturing

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.930
Winterfell, killing Rodrik, killing innocent
kids.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:34.779
He has suffered for his crimes – Ramsay
saw to that.

00:13:34.779 --> 00:13:37.310
And he’s tried to redeem himself by saving
Sansa.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:42.270
But he still feels guilt and feels torn between
Greyjoy and Stark.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:46.620
So Jon gives Theon the forgiveness and the
acceptance that he needs.

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:52.080
Says that Theon that he can be both a Greyjoy
and a Stark . So with his character conflict

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:57.190
fixed by a porque no los dos, Theon sets off
to save his sister Yara.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:14:03.730
But first, he has to win over his ironborn
crew, and he does it the way ironborn do – violence.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:08.029
On the one hand, it might feel kinda cheap
for Theon’s long and complex character arc

00:14:08.029 --> 00:14:10.450
to climax with a fistfight.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:15.699
But on the other hand, this scene really does
capture the meaning of Theon’s Greyjoy identity.

00:14:15.699 --> 00:14:21.380
He gets beaten down and defeated – but then
he rises again, harder and stronger . No matter

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:27.880
how bad he suffered, how bad he fucked up,
he can survive and persist and succeed.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:32.899
After the fight, Theon baptises himself with
saltwater, born again, like he was Season

00:14:32.899 --> 00:14:33.899
2.

00:14:33.899 --> 00:14:37.459
But this new identity he’s forged is stronger
than before.

00:14:37.459 --> 00:14:42.709
He gathers his twenty good men, and sets off
to save his sister.

00:14:42.709 --> 00:14:46.829
Sam arrives at Winterfell, and meets with
Bran – who he helped through the Wall back

00:14:46.829 --> 00:14:48.500
in Season 3.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:53.100
Bran says he remembers everything , and he
confirms the biggest oldest secret in Game

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:59.260
of Thrones – that Jon Snow is the child
of Rhaegar Targaryen and Lyanna Stark.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:04.140
Rhaegar is Daenerys’ brother, and Lyanna
is Ned’s sister.

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:08.320
Twenty years before the main story, Rhaegar
ran off with Lyanna, even though Rhaegar was

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:13.130
married to Elia Martell, and Lyanna was promised
to marry Robert Baratheon.

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:18.250
So Robert started a war against the Targaryens,
killing Rhaegar, usurping King Aerys, and

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.780
making himself king.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:22.210
Lyanna died giving birth in Dorne.

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:26.600
And Ned Stark came home with baby Jon Snow
and claimed Jon was his bastard, in order

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:31.230
to protect Jon – because Robert would have
killed him if he knew he was the son of a

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.230
Targaryen.

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:35.820
So that’s the R+L=J theory, and readers
have known about this for years.

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:40.560
But Sam says something that not even Bran
knew – that Rhaegar annulled his marriage

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:46.450
to Elia Martell and secretly married Lyanna,
meaning that Jon is not a bastard, but a legitimate

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:52.029
child of Prince Rhaegar, which means Jon’s
the rightful heir to the Iron Throne – ahead

00:15:52.029 --> 00:15:53.500
of Daenerys.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.480
A lot of readers suspected this too – there
are heaps of hints in the books that Jon would

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:01.920
be king . And people have speculated for years
about a secret marriage.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:05.240
One idea was that they would be married on
the Isle of Faces, because that’s near where

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:08.510
Lyanna met Rhaegar, and it has a bunch of
weirwood trees.

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:13.579
Weirwoods are used in northern marriage ceremonies,
and greenseers like Bran can see through weirwoods

00:16:13.579 --> 00:16:14.820
for their visions.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.860
So maybe this’ll be how we learn of the
marriage in the books.

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:21.570
But this idea of annulment raises questions.

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:25.511
In the books, it seems as though you can only
annul a marriage if it’s unconsummated – if

00:16:25.511 --> 00:16:28.009
the husband and wife haven’t had sex.

00:16:28.009 --> 00:16:30.230
Rhaegar and Elia had two kids.

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:32.830
So could their marriage be annulled?

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:36.850
Maybe in the books, Rhaegar will just marry
Lyanna in addition to Elia.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:39.839
The Targaryens do have a history of polygamy.

00:16:39.839 --> 00:16:45.080
But another weird twist is that Jon Snow’s
real name is Aegon Targaryen.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:49.630
Aegon is a popular name cause it’s the name
of the Conqueror, who first took over Westeros

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:51.920
and founded the Targaryen dynasty.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:56.300
But the weird thing is that one of Rhaegar’s
other children, by his first wife Elia, is

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:58.009
also named Aegon.

00:16:58.009 --> 00:17:02.820
So Rhaegar’s three children are named Rhaenys,
Aegon, and Aegon.

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:03.889
Why?

00:17:03.889 --> 00:17:07.839
One possible reason is that Rhaegar seemed
to be naming his children after Aegon the

00:17:07.839 --> 00:17:11.760
Conqueror and his two sisters, Rhaenys and
Visenya.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:17.250
Rhaegar was really into prophecy, and thought
his first son Aegon would be Azor Ahai, maybe

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:22.819
with his two other children, Rhaenys and Visenya
forming the three heads of the dragon, another

00:17:22.819 --> 00:17:24.370
prophetic thing.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:28.260
Point is, he might have expected his child
with Lyanna to be a daughter, and to name

00:17:28.260 --> 00:17:29.260
her Visenya.

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:33.300
But when Rhaegar died, and Jon turned out
male, Lyanna would have had to come up with

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:34.610
a new name.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:39.110
And by that time, Rhaegar’s first son Aegon
was dead – so Lyanna might as well name

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:44.299
this new kid Aegon – for the Conqueror,
and maybe to commemorate the dead Aegon.

00:17:44.299 --> 00:17:47.169
But it might still be a different name in
the books.

00:17:47.169 --> 00:17:52.789
Some people think Aemon, as a parallel to
Jon’s mentor – and ancestor – Maester

00:17:52.789 --> 00:17:53.789
Aemon.

00:17:53.789 --> 00:17:58.260
Or maybe Jaehaerys, one of the better Targaryen
kings, whose name starts with the same letter

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.410
as Jon.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:04.870
But they say a blue winter rose by any name
still smells as sweet . So maybe the name

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:06.160
is unimportant.

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:10.370
What matters is that Jon is half Stark, and
half Targaryen.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:15.250
Which connects nicely to what Jon told Theon
earlier – just as Theon can be a Stark and

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:19.880
a Greyjoy, Jon can be a Stark and a Targaryen.

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:23.960
We also get our first glimpse of Jon’s father,
Rhaegar Targaryen.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:28.450
He’s perhaps not as pretty as he’s described
in the books , but he does look a lot like

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:30.309
his brother Viserys.

00:18:30.309 --> 00:18:33.490
Maybe Viserys was imitating his brother’s
look.

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:38.260
Bran explains that Rhaegar and Lyanna were
in love – Rhaegar didn’t kidnap and rape

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.590
her, like Robert Baratheon claimed.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:44.450
And so, Bran says, Robert’s Rebellion was
based on a lie.

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:49.039
Which might not be quite true – Rhaegar
and Lyanna weren’t the only cause of the

00:18:49.039 --> 00:18:50.039
war.

00:18:50.039 --> 00:18:54.140
You could argue it really began when King
Aerys killed Rickard and Brandon Stark, and

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:59.330
demanded the heads of Robert and Ned . But
still, this misunderstanding adds tragedy

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:04.880
to Lyanna and Rhaegar’s relationship – star-crossed
lovers from opposing houses who both died

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:05.880
young.

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:10.710
But before we get too rosy-eyed, remember
we still know almost nothing about Lyanna

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.669
and Elia’s perspectives here.

00:19:12.669 --> 00:19:18.240
It sure looks like Elia was screwed over by
Rhaegar, and that Lyanna was a teenager who

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:22.530
Rhaegar locked in a tower and used to produce
a prophecy baby.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:27.080
So in the books at least, there’s still
a lot to be explored about these relationships.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:33.659
While Jon’s cousin Bran explains Jon’s
parents, Jon has sex with his aunt Daenerys

00:19:33.659 --> 00:19:36.860
– which is a lotta weird layers of incest.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:40.060
Tyrion listens outside, and looks concerned.

00:19:40.060 --> 00:19:43.610
He might be jealous of Jon – everyone’s
a bit in love with Daenerys.

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:48.700
But he might also worry that romance between
Dany and Jon could complicate the political

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.030
situation.

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:54.130
As Aemon once said, “What is honor compared
to a woman’s love?”

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.240
If you’re in love with someone, you might
make decisions based on what’s best for

00:19:57.240 --> 00:19:59.850
them instead of what’s best for the kingdom.

00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:04.139
In Book 5, Barristan thinks of all the loves
throughout history that have caused conflict

00:20:04.139 --> 00:20:09.520
– including Rhaegar and Lyanna’s . So
maybe Tyrion sees that Jon and Dany’s relationship

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.929
could be destructive.

00:20:10.929 --> 00:20:15.990
But, as Rhaegar knew, you can’t fulfil a
prophecy of ice and fire to save the world

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:18.660
without breaking a few Aegs.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:23.010
At Eastwatch, Tormund and Beric chill on the
Wall, when the Night King arrives with his

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:26.000
army – and with his dragon.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:31.780
Viserion breathes “blue fire” on the icy
Wall , and it starts to crack.

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:34.460
The Wall has stood for some eight thousand
years.

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:38.720
Built by the first men, children and giants
to protect the living from the dead , it’s

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:44.179
one of the “hinges of the world” . In
Book 1, Jon thinks if the Wall falls, the

00:20:44.179 --> 00:20:48.360
world falls with it . And now, the Wall falls.

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:52.890
There is nothing between the army of the dead
and Westeros.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:57.070
The fact that the Night King uses Viserion
to take down the Wall supports the idea that

00:20:57.070 --> 00:21:00.640
the lake scene last episode was a trap to
take Dany’s dragons.

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:05.309
Cause otherwise, the Night King was marching
on Eastwatch with no apparent plan to pass

00:21:05.309 --> 00:21:06.380
the Wall.

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:11.450
So maybe, the Night King, like Bran, is some
kinda greenseer, who can have visions of the

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:12.970
future and past.

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:17.040
His power must be limited – he’d win all
the time if he knew everything.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:21.299
But this definitely makes him even more dangerous.

00:21:21.299 --> 00:21:24.520
Some people think that Bran and the Night
King are the same person.

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:29.190
Like, that Bran went back in time and warged
into this guy who became the Night King, and

00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:34.429
lived as a white walker for thousands of years,
and is now battling the past version of himself

00:21:34.429 --> 00:21:38.280
– which might help explain the psychic connection
between the two.

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:43.549
It’s a fun idea, but there’s no real evidence,
and it’d require a level of time-travel-fuckery

00:21:43.549 --> 00:21:46.980
that might not really fit the story of Thrones
as we know it.

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:50.730
So it’s a cool idea, but isn’t likely.

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:54.370
Finally, some people are worried that Beric
and Tormund might have died here.

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:57.070
But it looks like they run to safety along
the Wall.

00:21:57.070 --> 00:22:01.520
Beric’s been talking about destiny so much
there’s no way he’s dying off-screen.

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:05.400
And Tormund’s gotta survive to make giant
blond babies with Brienne, right?

00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:11.240
So they’ll prolly be back in Season 8 – but
who else will?

00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:16.740
Game of Thrones Season 7 killed the Freys,
the Sand Snakes, the Tarlys, Olenna, Thoros,

00:22:16.740 --> 00:22:18.440
Benjen, and Littlefinger.

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:23.700
So basically all the lords of the south are
dead, along with some other loose ends.

00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:28.980
This lets Season 8 focus on the main conflicts
further north – between Cersei and Daenerys,

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:31.460
and between the living and the dead.

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:36.409
Almost all the named characters are in the
north or heading there – the Starks, Sansa

00:22:36.409 --> 00:22:37.409
Arya and Bran.

00:22:37.409 --> 00:22:39.100
The northern lords, like Lyanna.

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:40.140
Brienne and Podrick.

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:41.150
Sam and Gilly.

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:43.309
Davos, Gendry, and the Hound.

00:22:43.309 --> 00:22:45.260
Dolorous Edd with the Night’s Watch.

00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:47.380
Beric and Tormund at Eastwatch.

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:53.280
And Dany’s crew – Tyrion, Varys, Jorah,
Missandei, Grey Worm with the Unsullied, and

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:54.280
the Dothraki.

00:22:54.280 --> 00:22:56.049
Jaime, and probably Bronn.

00:22:56.049 --> 00:22:59.840
All who’s left south with Cersei is Qyburn
and the Mountain.

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:04.460
Euron’s heading to Essos to get the Golden
Company, with the help of the Iron Bank.

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:09.169
Theon’s out to save Yara, who might be at
the Iron Islands with Aeron?

00:23:09.169 --> 00:23:11.409
Or travelling with Euron maybe.

00:23:11.409 --> 00:23:16.680
And Melisandre’s in Volantis, maybe with
some other red priests, she said that she’d

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:17.680
return.

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:23.250
There are others who we might see again – there’s
Meera in the Neck, the maesters at Oldtown,

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:27.980
and Robin Arryn, who rules the Vale, represented
in the north by Bronze Yohn Royce.

00:23:27.980 --> 00:23:32.929
We don’t know what’s happening in the
riverlands, but maybe we’ll see Edmure again?

00:23:32.929 --> 00:23:37.860
The reach, stormlands and Dorne are a big
question mark, maybe Cersei will take em all

00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:39.809
back while Dany’s gone.

00:23:39.809 --> 00:23:44.679
We prolly won’t see Ellaria, or Daario,
or Illyrio, or Quaithe – we’ll hopefully

00:23:44.679 --> 00:23:46.020
see Ghost.

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:50.570
But what this basically comes down to is all
of these people in the north against the dead,

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:53.390
and against Queen Cersei.

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:58.920
The time is done for complicated politics,
for whole episodes devoted to walking and

00:23:58.920 --> 00:23:59.920
talking.

00:23:59.920 --> 00:24:04.490
The show has just six episodes left – to
give satisfying ends to all these character

00:24:04.490 --> 00:24:07.820
arcs, to answer big mysteries like Azor Ahai.

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:14.750
To decide who’ll live and who’ll die,
to bring an end to the song of ice and fire.

00:24:14.750 --> 00:24:17.710
Thanks for watching – this video, and this
series.

